{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-02–RP-06 derisk research is complete against tree\n`b0aac2314b63fc937b3f1d7d638a97609782e954`. Recovery authority remains\n`irascible-clueless-basenji` (`ee98-a2c0-7d12-4c75`). No production or tracked file changed, and no\nimplementation epic/story was created before the remaining approvals.\n\nDecision-ready briefs:\n\n- RP-02: `.joe-janitor/rp02-binding-store-research.md`; one recovery-semantics clarification.\n  The recovered approval explicitly wanted one fail-closed transaction, but research disproved the\n  premise that the current retirement path/ADR already provided multi-file atomicity. A real-file\n  probe proved a narrower journal-free option: after the current tombstone-first/live-second cut,\n  complete only an exact tombstone/forward/reverse identity overlap at the validated live-operation\n  boundary; repeat is a no-op and ambiguity aborts. Alternatives are structural parity that leaves\n  repair to RP-03, or a versioned general journal. Tickets-branch publication stays at the selective\n  orchestration seam; `gnatty-comparable-ynambu` already disproved the broad `git add -A` publisher.\n- RP-03: `.joe-janitor/rp03-outbound-lifecycle-research.md`; two choices remain. The scoped breaker\n  recommendation now preserves Jira's reason-qualified 429 scopes: global/tenant quota aborts,\n  endpoint burst stops only that mutation family, per-issue write stays ticket-local, and unknown\n  429 plus timeout/connect/5xx opens after 3 consecutive exhausted operations across at least 2\n  tickets. The second choice is label-first bounded containment after Jira create succeeds but key\n  persistence fails. A property-only crash/restart probe cannot recover; `rebar-id:<local_id>` can.\n  Manifest direction and dependency edges are fixed by the approved TicketPlan/one-story design.\n- RP-04: `.joe-janitor/rp04-composition-readback.md`; no new architectural choice. The approved\n  explicit > environment > project > user > default precedence, per-operation snapshot, separate\n  secret/provider boundary, non-secret subprocess envelope, central defaults, CI ownership gate,\n  and hosted canaries are supported. The story must explicitly name the CLI-over-environment\n  tracker precedence correction, malformed-config fail-closed behavior, captured backend settings,\n  custom layout/remote propagation, and removal of Cloud's adapter-local `DIG` fallback.\n- RP-05: `.joe-janitor/rp05-cli-registry-research.md`; one public-help choice remains. The lazy\n  registry/capability boundary is supported. Decide whether to normalize all 21 visible advanced\n  verbs onto side-effect-free package-data help now (recommended) or preserve the current two-family\n  help policy. Current `rebar help <advanced>` is unknown, and `enrich --help` entered execution.\n- RP-06: `.joe-janitor/rp06-review-kernel-research.md`, with authoritative chronology/failure\n  correction in `.joe-janitor/rp06-chronology-failure-critique.md`; one choice remains. The approved\n  effective applicability reversal, effective built-in/project-DET routing, and authored explicit\n  budget enforcement are settled; scheduler/cache modes preserve each gate. Choose parity-first\n  current-run failure projection (recommended) or normalize blocking-capable coverage gaps now.\n  Failed/cancelled/shed units never become success checkpoints under either option; the probe proved\n  today's transient failure is persisted as `[]` and suppresses a later healthy call.\n\nBehavior classification is explicit in `.joe-janitor/rp01-rp06-decision-audit.md`: each observable\nis PRESERVE, APPROVED DELTA, CORRECTIVE-TO-CONFIRM-WITH-RP, CHOICE PENDING, or DEPENDENCY CONSTRAINT.\nThe consolidated dependency/test plan is `.joe-janitor/rp01-rp06-derisk-index.md`.\n\nExecutable/read-back evidence:\n\n- RP-02 exact-overlap recovery probe passed; focused lifecycle/recovery tests and the commit/fsck\n  loop are recorded, with one isolated pre-existing path-loader fixture drift explicitly excluded.\n- RP-03 crash/restart containment and 429-scope probes passed; 32 historical lifecycle/apply tests,\n  24 persistence/fail-loud tests, and the broader 2,764-test reconciler corpus are recorded.\n- RP-04 operation-snapshot probe reproduced canonical `cli-store` versus public `env-store`,\n  malformed-config split, same-backend project reload, zero factory reads of supplied config, 19\n  ambient-loader modules, and 7 hard-coded tracker-path modules; 64 targeted and 86 broader\n  config/factory/DC/preflight tests passed.\n- RP-05 probe reproduced 19 policy sets, 54 help-backed commands, 21 advanced gaps, and zero tested\n  eager heavy imports; 113 focused tests and generated-reference check passed.\n- RP-06 effective-policy and failed-checkpoint probes passed; the focused gate/editor/runtime suites\n  and clean complexity ratchet are recorded in the briefs.\n\nCross-RP constraints: RP-03 depends on RP-02 and RP-04; RP-04 supplies RP-01/RP-03/RP-05's resolved\noperation authority; RP-01 owns runtime retry/accounting beneath RP-06 but RP-06 can migrate through\nthe stable runner seam without a hard tracker dependency. All behavior changes must appear as\nexpected deltas in the eventual stories rather than being hidden under “parity.”"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786917080936010001,"uuid":"535d336b-b4a7-466c-96e1-776a7fbf14b6"}